# Adjudicated closing claims in published commit messages.
#
# Read scripts/check-commit-verbs.sh before adding a line. The rules it enforces and the rules it
# trusts are different, and both are stated here so a reviewer can tell them apart:
#
#   mechanical   a waiver must name a full commit sha and the EXACT number set the report prints. A
#                line naming fewer numbers leaves the report failing; one naming more is stale and
#                also leaves it failing.
#   mechanical   every waiver is reprinted on every run. Nothing here is silently skipped.
#   by review    a claim is waivable only once its message is PUBLISHED. History on this repository
#                is never rewritten (AGENTS.md: `git revert`, never a force-push; every merge is a
#                merge commit), so before publication the remedy is to rewrite the message, not to
#                write a line here. Only the reviewer sees whether that order was respected.
#   by review    the reason must say what was read back. A waiver without a read-back is a guess.
#
# Format: <full-sha> <comma-separated numbers, ascending> <one-line reason>. Blank and `#` lines are
# comments. One entry per commit, on one line, because the reprint prints that line verbatim.
